  "title": "Early recovery arm made ship-safer by BLE advertising-enable disarm",
  "scope": "Keep unconditional early arm; add first-party disarm at HciLeSetAdvEnableCmd(1). Rebuild Apollo-main. Version-match NOR paired Renode with CHIPREV=0x22 fixture. No hardware flash. Crash-loop gate left unwired.",
  "choice": {
    "selected": "also_disarm_at_ble_advertising_enable",
    "rejected": "replace_early_arm_with_crash_loop_gate",
    "reason": "The 2 Nov 2026 diagnosis and hook comments already recommended an advertising disarm so out-of-case temples do not stay armed. The first-party enable=1 sites and the sim path that emits HCI 010A200101 (audio_ble_dm_adv_start_4b9e88) are known. The crash-loop gate remains intentionally unwired: the bricked temples' reset signature was never captured, and an early hang may never increment a watchdog streak. Replacing the early arm with that gate would drop recovery for a hang that never reaches a WDT reset."
  },
